We talk a lot on this podcast about the fascinating research conducted by psychological scientists. Today we're going to do something a little different. We're going to explore how that research gets done and how it might be done better. Over the past decade, there has been discussion of what critics have called psychology's reproducibility crisis. The fact that some published research results, including some classic findings in psychology, don't always hold up when other researchers reproduce those experiments. Now psychologists are leading a movement to address that problem by changing the way that research studies get conducted and published. So what exactly is reproducibility and why is it important? If the goal of science is to increase our understanding of the world,
在本期播客中，我们经常讨论心理学科学家所进行的迷人研究。今天我们要换个方式聊点不一样的。我们将探讨这些研究是如何完成的，以及如何才能做得更好。在过去的十年里，人们一直在讨论批评者所称的心理学可重复性危机。这就是一些已发表的研究结果，包括心理学中的一些经典发现，在其他研究人员重复这些实验时并不总是经得起检验。现在，心理学家们正在引领一场运动，通过改变研究的设计和发表方式来解决这个问题。那么，到底什么是可重复性，为什么它如此重要？如果科学的目标是增进我们对世界的理解，

