00:01:23.000 --> 00:02:05.000
psychology at the University of Virginia. Much of his own lab research has focused on implicit cognition, thoughts and feelings that occur outside of our conscious control. Broadly, he's interested in the gap between values and practices, between what people intend to do and what they actually do. Thank you for joining us today, Dr. Nosek. I'm delighted to be here today. Thank you for having me. Let's start with how you became interested in the reproducibility of scientific research. I know there were a series of events around 10 years ago that spurred a heightened scrutiny of psychological research and led to a lot of the work you're doing now. And I'm thinking in particular of cases such as psychologist Deutrick Stappell and Daryl Bem. Can you tell us what happened?
心理学教授。他实验室的大部分研究都集中在内隐认知上，即在我们有意识控制之外发生的思想和情感。广阔地说，他关注的是价值观与实践之间的差距，也就是人们意图做的事情与他们实际做的事情之间的差距。非常感谢您今天加入我们，诺塞克博士。我很高兴今天能来到这里。谢谢你们邀请我。让我们从您是如何对科学研究的可重复性产生兴趣开始聊起。我知道在大约10年前，有一系列事件引发了对心理学研究的更高程度的审视，并促成了您现在正在做的许多工作。我特别想到的一些案例，比如心理学家迪德里克·斯塔佩尔（Diederik Stapel）和达里尔·贝姆（Daryl Bem）。您能告诉我们发生了什么吗？

