of it, trying to say, oh, here's some things that you might trust, might not trust. So just that work itself is hard because you had to write down what you did. I have to interpret what you did, and I have to come to some understanding in the process. But let's say I'm really good at it as a reviewer. It's also really hard because it isn't transparent. All I have to review of what you did is what you wrote down. So taking that example of, of these many different analyses that you might do and just report the ones that make the finding come out but actually increase its false positive rate,
试图说：“哦，这里有些东西你可以信任，有些可能不能信任。”所以单单这项工作本身就很困难，因为你必须写下你所做的事情，而我必须解读你所做的事情，并在这一过程中达成某种理解。但假设我作为一个审稿人非常擅长此道。这也真的很困难，因为它并不透明。我所能审查的关于你所做的事情，仅仅是你写下来的内容。因此，拿这个例子来说，你可能会做许多不同的分析，却只报告那些让研究结果成立的分析，但这实际上增加了假阳性率，

