00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:45.000
well, he knows how to write a paper. And how am I to know that the data aren't there, aren't real, if I can't access the data? So one of the big limitations of the peer review process, besides not in being imperfect, and that's just part of the system, no system like that will be perfect because science is hard, and it takes a while to figure things out. But one of the big barriers for effective peer review and ultimately self-correction is a lack of transparency. If you can't see what I did, how I did, can't see the data that I generated, then there's very little chance that you can effectively evaluate the quality of my work.
嗯，他知道如何撰写论文。如果我无法访问数据，我又怎么知道数据不在那里、不是真实的呢？因此，同行评议过程的一大局限性（除了它本身并不完美之外，这只是系统的一部分，没有任何这样的系统会是完美的，因为科学很难，弄清楚事情需要时间）在于缺乏透明度。如果你看不到我做了什么、我是怎么做的，也看不到我生成的数据，那么你几乎没有可能有效地评估我工作的质量。

