00:21:49.000 --> 00:22:34.000
So as a consequence of that, there has been a very, broad engagement in the psychological community by bottom-up researchers themselves saying, we need to change this, and so we're going to start to adopt some of these new behaviors, sharing data, pre-registering research, and otherwise, and some top-down, where publishers and editors, funders, and institutions are saying we need to change our reward systems, how it is that we encourage the most credible research that we can. Now, it's 10 years since some of those eliciting events occur that may brought this really to the fore. And it's, you know, culture change takes a long time, but a lot has changed.
